{"id":"eb5cb1ee-5ea9-4b06-b0fb-4ac9b0b28d21","object":"response","created_at":1792378502,"status":"completed","background":false,"completed_at":1792378505,"content_filters":null,"error":null,"frequency_penalty":0.0,"incomplete_details":null,"instructions":null,"max_output_tokens":4096,"max_tool_calls":null,"model":"deepseek-flash","moderation":null,"output":[{"type":"message","id":"b7fa2c46-3ad4-4ded-af97-87f420ddfefb","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"output_text","annotations":[],"logprobs":[],"text":"{\"resource_type\": \"explanation\", \"prompt_version\": \"learning-resources-v1\", \"content\": {\"markdown\": \"# 单链表头插法\\n\\n## 三个基本概念\\n\\n- **节点 (node)**：由数据域 `data` 和指针域 `next` 组成的结构体变量，是链表的基本单元。\\n- **头指针 (head)**：指向链表第一个节点的指针。头指针本身不是节点；当 `head == NULL` 时，链表为空。\\n- **头插法 (head insertion)**：每次把新节点插到链表最前端，使它成为新的第一个节点，并让 `head` 指向它。\\n\\n空链表写作：\\n\\n```\\nhead -> NULL\\n```\\n\\n## 头插法的核心两步\\n\\n设新节点为 `new_node`，头插法只需两步：\\n\\n```c\\nnew_node->next = head;  /* 新节点接到原链表前面 */\\nhead = new_node;        /* 头指针改指向新节点 */\\n```\\n\\n顺序不能颠倒：必须先让新节点接上原链表，再移动 `head`，否则原链表会丢失。\\n\\n## 用同一个例子走一遍\\n\\n从空链表 `head -> NULL` 开始，依次头插 1、2、3。\\n\\n**插入 1**：`new_node->next = head`（即 NULL），`head = new_node`。\\n\\n```\\nhead -> [1] -> NULL\\n```\\n\\n**插入 2**：`new_node->next = head`（指向 [1]），`head = new_node`。\\n\\n```\\nhead -> [2] -> [1] -> NULL\\n```\\n\\n**插入 3**：`new_node->next = head`（指向 [2]），`head = new_node`。\\n\\n```\\nhead -> [3] -> [2] -> [1] -> NULL\\n```\\n\\n**遍历**：`p = head`，沿 `next` 依次打印，得到输出 `3 2 1`。\\n\\n**释放**：`p = head`，循环中先保存 `next`，再 `free(p)`，最后 `head = NULL`。\\n\\n## 为什么输出顺序与插入顺序相反\\n\\n头插法每次都把新节点放在最前面，所以最后插入的节点离 `head` 最近，遍历时最先被访问。插入顺序是 1、2、3，遍历顺序就是 3、2、1。\\n\\n## 小结\\n\\n- 头指针指向第一个节点，空链表用 `NULL` 表示。\\n- 头插法固定两步：先 `new_node->next = head`，再 `head = new_node`。\\n- 头插法得到的链表顺序与插入顺序相反。\"}}"}],"phase":"final_answer","role":"assistant"}],"parallel_tool_calls":true,"presence_penalty":0.0,"previous_response_id":null,"prompt_cache_key":null,"prompt_cache_retention":null,"reasoning":{"effort":"none","summary":null},"safety_identifier":null,"service_tier":"default","store":false,"temperature":0.0,"text":{"format":{"type":"json_schema","name":"edumind_result","schema":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["resource_type","prompt_version","content"],"properties":{"resource_type":{"const":"explanation"},"prompt_version":{"const":"learning-resources-v1"},"content":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["markdown"],"properties":{"markdown":{"type":"string","minLength":1}}}}},"description":null,"strict":null},"verbosity":null},"tool_choice":"auto","tools":[],"top_logprobs":0,"top_p":1.0,"truncation":"disabled","usage":{"input_tokens":1974,"input_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0},"output_tokens":636,"output_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":0},"total_tokens":2610},"user":null,"metadata":{}}